        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-18T11:04:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not ideal because even if the messages were successfully sent to the handler, the handler may have failed to send them to the VM over UDC. the vm might be dead for example, or the UDC connection may be broken.\n\nsince we can\u0027t use return value of this method for the failure of handler sending the events to the VM, we should use a callback.\n\nif we use callback to report the result of sending events to VM, we should use it universally - even for the failures made here. otherwise, users have to distinguish these two types of failures.",
      "parentUuid": "227f3ad0_33b7cd8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 996,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 996,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "0f3db58badd5e2ca3d5c8a375f77035ca03e03c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b57dc8b8_7238d7e2",
        "filename": "java/framework/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 996,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081223
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-18T11:07:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think a callback will be enough in most cases as those events are coming from different views, so the app itself would need to then dispatch them to the original view...\n\nThe failure to send the message to the handler should be covered now, vsock is harder for this reason",
      "parentUuid": "e814d94a_8b8a0924",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 996,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 996,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "0f3db58badd5e2ca3d5c8a375f77035ca03e03c0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
